      "difficulty_reason": "The authors derive the nonconstant-weight innovation kernel and variance recurrence for the weighted recursive-tree process, establish the needed square-summability under p_n=O(1/n) without a polynomial cumulative-weight asymptotic, and control the global remainder to obtain a nondegenerate almost-sure/L2 linear-scale limit with a positive quadratic variance coefficient. The quoted martingale convergence/Kronecker facts alone do not give the model-specific representation and remainder estimates. Power-weight regimes, explicit constants and root-traversal costs are supporting specializations, not extra counts.",
